A fair number of classes can get to Basic in pickaxe.  Pickaxes
appear often in the mines and later.  Pickaxes dig so you're
often wielding one when surprised, often enough that you
generally can advance it.  Pickaxe and dwavish mattock are in
the same skill class and dwarvish mattock is the non-artifact
weapon that does the most damage.  All of these are reasonable
arguments to consider advancing pickaxe to Basic.  Maybe not
convincing arguments but that's a matter of tastes.  At least
very many characters carry a pickaxe in their bag of holding
most of the game and why not advance stuff you constantly carry?
By the time I've stormed the Castle mine has often been
rustproofed and sometimes even given some amount of plus
enchantment.

Except for Archeologist the above doesn't convince me it is
worth going past Basic in pickaxe whether your class is able to
or not.  I feel the same about much plus enchantment.  One
blessed scroll of enchant armor is plenty if and only if the
rest of my weaponry is maxed out.

